  "derivation": "The residual is E = (2g+g^2-r) + 2ug. With the linear reference g=r/2, E = r^2/4 + ur. The source-only body B(r) = -1/(2*(1+sqrt(1+r))^2) exactly cancels the pure remainder 2g+g^2-r when u=0, because r/2 - r^2/(2*(1+sqrt(1+r))^2) = sqrt(1+r)-1 (verified by the identity (1+sqrt(1+r))^2 - r = 2(1+sqrt(1+r))). For u != 0, the leading uncanceled term is 2u*(r/2) = ur. Setting C = -1/2 makes ur*C = -ur/2, so the 2*ur*C contribution to E cancels the 2u*(r/2) = ur term to leading order. The residual then reduces from O(r^2 + ur) to O(r^3 + r^2*u + r*u^2). Both bodies are smooth on an open neighborhood of [-1/4,1/4] x [-1/8,1/8] since 1+r >= 3/4 > 0 and 1+sqrt(1+r) > 0 throughout. No singularities, no max-clipping, no piecewise structure needed.",
